# Caller stub (Test Hardening C1) — logic lives in foundry/foundry-stocks;
# copier-shipped, stamped only when this star declared `critical_modules`.
#
# Coverage says a line RAN. Mutation says a line is TESTED: the gate breaks the
# source on purpose and fails when the suite does not notice.
#
# TWO FILES, NOT ONE — this one and mutation-nightly.yml. This stub used to be a
# single workflow carrying BOTH triggers, which the reusable workflow argues
# against at length and which none of the 24 hand-wired callers actually use:
# on a pull_request the scheduled job reports `skipped`, and a required check
# reporting anything other than success is the hazard ci.yml spends a paragraph
# on. One trigger per file, one status per event.
#
# NO paths-ignore, and its removal is the other half of the same fix. A
# filtered-out PR posts NO STATUS AT ALL, and a required check that never
# reports blocks its PR forever — the exact failure ci.yml warns about. The
# reusable workflow already no-ops internally when a PR touches none of the
# critical modules: the job still runs, and still reports success.
#
# WHAT THIS GATE JUDGES IS THE DIFF, not the repo. It mutates only the lines the
# PR added, so `fail-under` is a claim about the code you just wrote and says
# nothing about the module's legacy score. The whole-module number is the
# nightly's job.
#
# fail-under is 0 (report-only) at birth ON PURPOSE. Read the honest score off a
# few nightly runs first, then raise it here. A threshold nobody has measured is
# a threshold everyone learns to skip.
name: mutation

on:
  pull_request:

jobs:
  mutation:
    uses: foundry/foundry-stocks/.forgejo/workflows/mutation.yml@main
    with:
      critical-modules: "{{ critical_modules }}"
      mode: diff
      fail-under: 0
    # pragma comment: detect-secrets flags the word 'secrets' as a Secret Keyword,
    # and `secrets: inherit` is the reusable-workflow idiom, not a credential.
    secrets: inherit  # pragma: allowlist secret
